## Package and runtime reproducibility

The pinned package versions are:

* `@earendil-works/pi-agent-core`: `0.84.1`
* `@earendil-works/pi-ai`: `0.84.1` (protocol/type dependency)
* `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent`: `0.84.1` (default coding profile source)

The source root requires Node `>=22.19.0` (`package.json:engines.node`). The checkout was
inspected with Node `v26.5.0` and npm `11.7.0`; these are observations, not a new runtime
requirement. Dependency resolution is npm lockfile v3 from
`parity/upstream/source/package-lock.json` (SHA-256:
`01bb5df57ed0de4f308ed1b88b4536e43a0b61ce82b0eff3fcb1b922176c3c4c`). The source `.npmrc`
sets `save-exact=true` and `min-release-age=2`.

Install the locked fixture-runner dependencies from the pin with:

```text
cd parity/upstream/source
npm ci --ignore-scripts
```

At this checkout, `npm run build:offline` stops before completion because the source omits
`packages/ai/src/providers/data/amazon-bedrock.json` and its `check:model-data` script asks for
`npm run hydrate:model-data`. That model-catalog hydration is not required by the selected
agent/profile fixtures and must not become a hidden network prerequisite for parity.

The parity runner is an in-process TypeScript fixture. Invoke the checked-in runners directly
with `./node_modules/.bin/tsx ../<runner>.mts ...` from `parity/upstream/source`; they import the
selected SDK source modules and must not invoke the `pi` executable or any Pi CLI. No upstream CLI
runner was used to establish this pin.

